{
 "topic": "de.functional-dependencies-normal-forms",
 "voice": "breeze-mellow-v2",
 "asr": "large-v3-turbo",
 "clips": {
  "01": {
   "hash": "808020a596463661",
   "takes": [
    "5600174728c0e457101a",
    "24aa4d53f7c210556305"
   ],
   "duration": 10.542,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Same six rows of data, stored two different ways.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.1
    },
    {
     "text": "One of them is a single missed update away from telling you two different things at once.",
     "start": 4.52,
     "end": 10.192
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 148,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02": {
   "hash": "72fdeaf86c8c0a6e",
   "takes": [
    "6cd85113d8325619cf19",
    "b1b9f590ea0d303680e3"
   ],
   "duration": 8.432,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Splitting data apart to kill redundancy sounds like it has to cost you a join somewhere down the line.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.753
    },
    {
     "text": "Does it always?",
     "start": 7.173,
     "end": 8.082
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 157,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "02a": {
   "hash": "ad4ab065cab720e4",
   "takes": [
    "0edb4b84f4632f4a96bd",
    "e3024b3d7a5f354cec8b"
   ],
   "duration": 13.61,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "It depends entirely on how the data actually gets queried afterward.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.302
    },
    {
     "text": "A handful of point lookups barely notice a join. A query that scans everything pays for it on every single row.",
     "start": 4.722,
     "end": 13.26
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.0,
   "true_peak": -2.9,
   "wpm": 141,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "03": {
   "hash": "df2f3f5d78136807",
   "takes": [
    "3a1b0132d46150dc5d43",
    "880952fc813f9e98fb73"
   ],
   "duration": 11.204,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here is the actual rule underneath all of this.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.292
    },
    {
     "text": "One column determines another when every value on one side always comes with exactly the same value on the other.",
     "start": 3.712,
     "end": 10.854
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.1,
   "wpm": 155,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "04": {
   "hash": "df2f32590b52607d",
   "takes": [
    "878878b5138243826d0d",
    "59a8ee287a975bae2628"
   ],
   "duration": 10.799,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Start from one column, and let every rule that already applies keep firing.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.217
    },
    {
     "text": "Each firing switches on more columns, until nothing new switches on at all.",
     "start": 5.637,
     "end": 10.449
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.2,
   "true_peak": -3.1,
   "wpm": 144,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "05": {
   "hash": "e0fc0f1af143ecc8",
   "takes": [
    "3c60fe6cfaecb73777ce",
    "ca51757eb00cacf96ba0"
   ],
   "duration": 10.801,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That full set it eventually reaches is the whole point.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 3.838
    },
    {
     "text": "Whichever starting column gets you there, with nothing smaller able to do the same, is your real key.",
     "start": 4.258,
     "end": 10.451
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 156,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06": {
   "hash": "705cd5835a84c7a0",
   "takes": [
    "e647718ba56dd7fc6050",
    "74188b1886e3a6306b88"
   ],
   "duration": 8.091,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Now here is a column that clearly determines something else on its own.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.444
    },
    {
     "text": "Does that earn it the same status?",
     "start": 4.864,
     "end": 7.741
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.3,
   "true_peak": -2.2,
   "wpm": 148,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "06a": {
   "hash": "d4a102156838fd0b",
   "takes": [
    "a00237b192fd447cc5d7",
    "e342caef3a696c8ddb8a"
   ],
   "duration": 13.669,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "No, and the reason is mechanical, not a matter of opinion.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.426
    },
    {
     "text": "Its own reach stalls out early. It never gets anywhere near two of the other columns no matter how long you let it run.",
     "start": 4.846,
     "end": 13.319
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 154,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "07": {
   "hash": "37ad12fa5fd7ebc0",
   "takes": [
    "23501fd109cb271d1cb7",
    "8f99f3063dd2aca460fe"
   ],
   "duration": 11.534,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Trace it yourself and you will watch it stall in exactly the same place every time.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.296
    },
    {
     "text": "Determining one neighbor is not the same thing as determining the whole row.",
     "start": 6.716,
     "end": 11.184
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.2,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 151,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "08": {
   "hash": "ddd76616173c6f11",
   "takes": [
    "0f7ed2d5a2d1d4c229db",
    "187cbb6c1d10dabf8ba5"
   ],
   "duration": 19.16,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Climb the first three rungs of this ladder and each one is answering a different complaint.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.518
    },
    {
     "text": "Keep every value a single thing, then make sure nothing depends on only part of a key, then cut anything depending on a non-key column instead of the key itself.",
     "start": 5.938,
     "end": 18.81
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 147,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "09": {
   "hash": "c0414d2121bff8a8",
   "takes": [
    "ae354d4350de7331fb4f",
    "f4ba2d13a31e4ac786a7"
   ],
   "duration": 13.623,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "There is a gap the third rung quietly leaves open, and the next rung closes it.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.229
    },
    {
     "text": "Every single determining column now has to be a full key in its own right, not just determine something.",
     "start": 6.649,
     "end": 13.273
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.3,
   "true_peak": -2.7,
   "wpm": 154,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "10": {
   "hash": "4bec16d8d554d15f",
   "takes": [
    "bc8c9b207da02ee985d7",
    "d6b23ae749b4e43a58de"
   ],
   "duration": 13.495,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Up to here, every rule has been about one value picking out exactly one other value.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.625
    },
    {
     "text": "This next kind of rule is different: one value can pick out a whole independent set of others.",
     "start": 7.045,
     "end": 13.145
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 151,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "11": {
   "hash": "4736f396e810bb5d",
   "takes": [
    "d5562ccaab4c0ac151c8",
    "03b4bde0e26477c30e12"
   ],
   "duration": 15.643,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Split a table along one of these real rules, and something important is guaranteed.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 5.536
    },
    {
     "text": "Join the pieces back, and you get every original row back, exactly, with nothing lost and nothing invented.",
     "start": 5.956,
     "end": 15.293
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 123,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "12": {
   "hash": "e8a830a0b0f99438",
   "takes": [
    "d780a3c33f6f1bae23a6",
    "74dbdefd2817631373c4"
   ],
   "duration": 16.196,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That guarantee is not the only one worth keeping, and it is not automatic that you keep both.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 6.706
    },
    {
     "text": "You can satisfy it completely and still lose the ability to check an original rule without stitching things back together first.",
     "start": 7.126,
     "end": 15.846
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 144,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "13": {
   "hash": "84a2ac1728b0b39d",
   "takes": [
    "4fed8ff7cbaf24b4d703",
    "3568a1ee9b841faafb17"
   ],
   "duration": 16.083,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Watch what actually happens when the same change gets made two different ways.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.654
    },
    {
     "text": "One version needs a single touch. The other needs several, and skipping just one of them leaves two conflicting answers sitting on file at the same time.",
     "start": 5.074,
     "end": 15.733
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -1.8,
   "wpm": 149,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "14": {
   "hash": "6efa10bc089b0a8f",
   "takes": [
    "8508b7dd9de9963de54b",
    "629e14252f3a44516756"
   ],
   "duration": 16.763,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "None of that makes storing it the second way a mistake by itself.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 4.452
    },
    {
     "text": "A workload built around scanning everything pays a real cost on every row for a join the other version never needed, so trading some risk for speed can be exactly the right call.",
     "start": 4.872,
     "end": 16.413
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 165,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "15": {
   "hash": "656f7375b65724b9",
   "takes": [
    "2e7c8a5b523768d1e33b",
    "077c720e5f1e43df0edf"
   ],
   "duration": 14.461,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "One determining rule, one full reach, one real key. Four rungs, each closing a gap the last one left open.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.702
    },
    {
     "text": "One guarantee you never skip, and one you sometimes trade away on purpose for speed.",
     "start": 9.122,
     "end": 14.111
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.0,
   "wpm": 145,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "16": {
   "hash": "7a0c94ab3c6ec882",
   "takes": [
    "d969522d91a889a34370",
    "fc5818c28596b005e82b"
   ],
   "duration": 11.035,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Here is a new rule: one column determines every other column directly, with nothing else determining anything.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 8.043
    },
    {
     "text": "So what has to be the key?",
     "start": 8.463,
     "end": 10.685
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.4,
   "true_peak": -2.7,
   "wpm": 130,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  },
  "16a": {
   "hash": "722ef45d68d33551",
   "takes": [
    "c70350d8642cd018f2ca",
    "faef9fa44db0706dec04"
   ],
   "duration": 9.893,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "That one column, on its own.",
     "start": 0.15,
     "end": 2.389
    },
    {
     "text": "Its reach already covers everything in a single step, and nothing smaller could possibly do the same job.",
     "start": 2.809,
     "end": 9.543
    }
   ],
   "lufs": -16.5,
   "true_peak": -1.9,
   "wpm": 146,
   "wer": 0.0,
   "exact": true,
   "tolerated": []
  }
 }
}